bill@west.msi.com (Bill Poitras) writes:

>Todd Walk (walk@mrcnext.cso.uiuc.edu) wrote:
>: >The title line says it all. What routine should be added to which file
>: >if you want to limit the number of maximum users in NH3.1 on unix
>: >(to, say 20 or 30)? Please reply via email.
>: >Much thanks in advance if you do.
>: Could someone please post this?             
>
>From config.h:
>/*
> * If it is desirable to limit the number of people that can play Hack
> * simultaneously, define HACKDIR, SECURE and MAX_NR_OF_PLAYERS.
> * #define MAX_NR_OF_PLAYERS 6
> */
>
>Any questions?


It can also be done from the top lines of the nethack script which
calls the binary, by setting MAXNROFPLAYERS to the desired value.
This way, recompilation isn't necessary.  You have to be sure that
the binary is off-limits to most players, by making the script
setuid or setgid and closing off the playground (the way it
should be done, anyway).

